          <td style="background:#9ab3d4;color:#FFFFFF"><h3><strong>You Spoke, We Listened Resources Page</strong></h3></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="bodyBlue"><p><br><img src="../images/HL_YSWL.gif" alt="You Spoke, We Listened Resources Page" class="headlineGraphic2" align="left" />RTD Chief Operations Officer <strong>Michael Ford</strong> and his staff conducted <strong>Division Visits</strong> in January and February at each operating division, including <strong>Maintenance of Way, District Shops, East Metro, Platte</strong> and <strong>Boulder</strong> bus facilities and the Light Rail Operations facility, <strong>Elati</strong> twice – once at 3 a.m.!</p>
            <p>At each visit, Michael talked about RTD current events and <strong>Information Technology</strong> staff discussed the upcoming <strong>Information Gateway</strong> tool for communication and RTD’s new HR and payroll system, <strong>Workday</strong>, which will replace <strong>Oracle</strong> for <strong>Human Resources</strong> and payroll functions.</p>
            <p>Michael then opened the floor to employees. Employees were very candid, expressing frustrations and concerns, and telling him what is working and what needs improvement.</p>
            <p>To learn more about his visits, <a href="/operator/secure/fetchDocument.do?docName=/MMD/Monday_Morning_Dispatch 3.9.2020.pdf" class="landingPageLink">click here to read the article in the Monday Morning Dispatch</a>.</p>
            <p>The <strong>Communications</strong> team has identified six themes that came up consistently at each visit. Here are the notes and actions being taken for each topic.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>RECOGNITION</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <table width="100%" border="1" cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" summary="Nested table">
              <tbody>
